{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.window_is_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.window_is_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L118-L123","doc":"**Non-vacuity: the window is inhabited.** An affine multiplicity with a large negative\nintercept does give a positive three-body cumulant — here `α = 5`, `β = −8`, so `μ(2) = 2`,\n`μ(3) = 7` and `b₃ = 1 > 0`. So the affine family is not excluded; the measured intercept is what\nfails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_pos_forces_intercept_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_pos_forces_intercept_window","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L108-L116","doc":"**So the intercept is pinned to a window.** A positive two-body binding together with a\npositive three-body cumulant forces `−2α < β < −³⁄₂·α`: the intercept must be large and negative,\ncomparable to twice the slope. (The window is non-empty exactly when `α > 0`, which is not needed\nfor the implication itself.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L101-L106","doc":"**A positive three-body cumulant is exactly a bound on the intercept**: `b₃ > 0` iff\n`2β < −3α`, with no further hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_ratio_depends_only_on_intercept_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_ratio_depends_only_on_intercept_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L86-L93","doc":"**The ratio depends only on the intercept-to-slope ratio.** Writing `β = r·α` with `α ≠ 0`,\n`b₃/b₂ = −(3 + 2r)/(2 + r)` — the slope cancels. So the search for a carrier reproducing `b₃` is\none-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L82-L84","doc":"`b₂ = 2α + β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_affine_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_affine_eq","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L77-L80","doc":"**The cumulant of an affine multiplicity is exact and linear**: `b₃ = −(3α + 2β)`. The `A`\ndependence cancels entirely — only the slope and intercept survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L74-L75","doc":"The connected three-body cumulant: `b₃ = μ(3) − 3·μ(2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b2","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L71-L72","doc":"The two-body binding in count-multiplicity units: `b₂ = μ(2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.mu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.mu","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.lean#L68-L69","doc":"An affine count multiplicity `μ(A) = α·A + β`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}